    <string name="about">About</string>
    <string name="about_version">Version %s</string>
    <string name="about_body">Sawt+ turns your phone into a wireless microphone that streams live audio to a computer over Wi‑Fi, with USB/ADB as a fallback.\n\nBased on the original open-source project “audiosource” by gdzx. Streaming format: 16-bit PCM, 48 kHz, mono, 20 ms frames.</string>

    <string name="how_to_connect">How to connect</string>
    <string name="how_to_connect_body">1. Keep this phone on the same Wi‑Fi as the computer.\n2. On the computer run: sawt discover\n3. Pair with the 6‑digit code.\n4. The phone appears as a system microphone.\n\nUSB/ADB still works as a fallback: sawt adb run</string>

    <string name="hint">Keep the service running in the background. On Realme/Oppo, set Battery usage to Unrestricted so the system does not kill the microphone service.\n\nFirst time? Install this app once, then use Wi‑Fi from the PC client (`sawt discover`, or `sawt web`).</string>

